WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.361 --> 00:00:04.761
♪ (music) ♪

00:00:05.673 --> 00:00:07.316
Give me one minute and I'll show you

00:00:07.316 --> 00:00:09.000
how Cloud Armor could help protect

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.782
your applications and websites

00:00:10.782 --> 00:00:13.231
against [null] of service and web attacks.

00:00:13.681 --> 00:00:17.683
Cloud Armor is an enterprise-grade
DDoS defense service

00:00:17.683 --> 00:00:22.183
and web application firewall
that leverages Google's vast expertise

00:00:22.183 --> 00:00:24.745
in protecting key internet properties

00:00:24.745 --> 00:00:29.702
to provide built-in defense against
L3 and L4 DDoS attacks.

00:00:29.825 --> 00:00:33.721
Cloud Armor also allows you
to mitigate OWASP's top ten risks

00:00:33.721 --> 00:00:37.779
by providing pre-defined rules
to help you defend against its hacks,

00:00:37.779 --> 00:00:41.105
such as cross site scripting
and SQL injection attacks.

00:00:41.375 --> 00:00:44.896
Cloud Armor has IP-based
and Geo-based access controls

00:00:44.896 --> 00:00:48.383
so you can allow or deny traffic
based on the source

00:00:48.383 --> 00:00:51.847
and geo-location,
or filter your incoming traffic

00:00:51.847 --> 00:00:56.758
based on IPv4 and IPv6 addresses or CIDRs.

00:00:57.374 --> 00:00:59.588
Setting up Cloud Armor
is very straightforward.

00:00:59.588 --> 00:01:02.431
You'll find Cloud Armor
in the Google Cloud Console

00:01:02.431 --> 00:01:05.699
under the Networking/Network
Security section.

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:07.933
There, you can create a security policy

00:01:07.933 --> 00:01:10.922
and configure it to help you protect
your web application.

00:01:11.898 --> 00:01:13.957
The Standard pricing model is simple.

00:01:13.957 --> 00:01:16.532
It's a pay-as-you-go measuring
and charging

00:01:16.532 --> 00:01:19.552
for the security policies and rules
within that policy.

00:01:20.291 --> 00:01:22.466
Or you can choose
the Managed Protection Plus,

00:01:22.466 --> 00:01:25.901
a value-added service that starts
with Standards here,

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:28.180
then adds Adaptive Protection,

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:31.359
access to Google's DDoS response team,

00:01:31.609 --> 00:01:34.819
DDoS bill protection,
and other protection capabilities

00:01:34.819 --> 00:01:37.491
in a predictable subscription
pricing model.

00:01:38.141 --> 00:01:41.048
So next time you're looking to protect
your web applications,

00:01:41.048 --> 00:01:42.861
take a minute to look at Cloud Armor.

00:01:42.861 --> 00:01:44.401
To learn more, check out

00:01:44.401 --> 00:01:46.957
<i>cloud.google.com/armor.</i>

00:01:46.957 --> 00:01:51.345
♪ (music) ♪

